-- 2-butanol, the case where a methylene splits with no ring, no amine and no second functional group.
-- Atoms: 0 the first methyl carbon with hydrogens 1 to 3, 4 the carbinol carbon with hydrogen 5, 6 its
-- oxygen with hydrogen 7, 8 the methylene carbon with hydrogens 9 and 10, 11 the last methyl carbon with
-- hydrogens 12 to 14. The carbinol carbon is a stereocentre -- methyl, ethyl, hydroxyl, hydrogen, all
-- four different -- so the two methylene hydrogens next to it are diastereotopic.
num-but-obs : List Nat
num-but-obs = cons 1 (cons 2 (cons 3 (cons 5 (cons 9 (cons 10 (cons 12 (cons 13 (cons 14 nil))))))))
